# Google Cloud compute / GKE

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Compute Engine VMs, disks, instance groups, or
GKE clusters/node pools. Prefer authenticated `gcloud`. Skip when the ask is
only in-cluster pods/events/logs after credentials exist — that surface is
out of scope for this plugin.

## Transport

No Google Cloud MCP discovered. Use `gcloud`. If a Cloud MCP becomes ready,
prefer its inventory tools — do not invent tool names.

## Resolve ids

Never invent instance name, zone, cluster, location, or node-pool name.
Resolve from the user, a prior list this turn, or:

| Need | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List VMs | `gcloud compute instances list --project=PROJECT` |
| Describe VM | `gcloud compute instances describe NAME --zone=ZONE --project=PROJECT` |
| List disks | `gcloud compute disks list --project=PROJECT` |
| Describe disk | `gcloud compute disks describe NAME --zone=ZONE --project=PROJECT` |
| List MIGs | `gcloud compute instance-groups managed list --project=PROJECT` |
| List GKE clusters | `gcloud container clusters list --project=PROJECT` |
| Describe cluster | `gcloud container clusters describe NAME --location=LOCATION --project=PROJECT` |
| List node pools | `gcloud container node-pools list --cluster=CLUSTER --location=LOCATION --project=PROJECT` |

If several match, list candidates and ask once — do not pick prod by vibes.

## Status receipts

For VMs report: name, zone, status (`RUNNING` / `TERMINATED` / …), machine
type, and primary internal/external IP when present.

For GKE report: name, location, status, master version, node-pool count /
versions, and network when relevant. Do not claim healthy without a fresh
describe/list this turn.

## Mutate (gated)

Create / start / stop / reset / resize / upgrade need an **explicit verb**
this turn naming the resource. Examples (only when authorized):

| Action | Command shape |
| --- | --- |
| Start / stop VM | `gcloud compute instances start\|stop NAME --zone=ZONE` |
| Reset VM | `gcloud compute instances reset NAME --zone=ZONE` |
| Resize MIG | `gcloud compute instance-groups managed resize …` |
| Get kubeconfig | `gcloud container clusters get-credentials NAME --location=LOCATION` (fine for authorized triage setup) |
| Cluster upgrade | `gcloud container clusters upgrade …` — irreversible risk; follow `google-cloud-safety` |

Delete of VMs, disks, MIGs, or clusters → `google-cloud-safety` plus an
explicit delete verb naming each resource.

## Defaults

1. Read-only status is the default (list/describe).
2. Always pass `--project` (and zone/location) once resolved — do not rely on
   a silent config default the user did not confirm.
3. Prefer `--format=yaml` or a tight table for one object; summarize lists.
4. After GKE context is known, in-cluster pod/event/log triage is **out of
   scope** here — stop or hand the operator the cluster name/location only.
5. Do not open firewall rules or expose ports as a side effect of compute
   work — that is `google-cloud-iam-network` with an explicit ask.

## Symptom hints (control plane)

| Signal | Likely check |
| --- | --- |
| VM `TERMINATED` / unexpected stop | describe + recent operations (`gcloud compute operations list`) |
| Cannot SSH | network tags / firewall / OS Login — see iam-network; do not punch holes |
| GKE `RECONCILING` / `ERROR` | cluster describe conditions + node-pool status |
| Node pool stuck upgrading | node-pools describe; do not force unless asked |
| Quota errors on create | `gcloud compute project-info describe` / regions — report quota name |

## Refuse

- Deleting VMs, disks, snapshots, or clusters without safety + explicit delete.
- Opening firewall or public IPs beyond what the user named.
- Inventing zones, machine types, or image families.
- Pasting service-account keys used by instances into chat.
